    <string name="installers_description"><b><big>Normal (Rootless) Installe</big></b>r
Uses Android's built-in package manager to install applications. This method does not require special privileges but needs user confirmation for each installation. It's the safest and most compatible option.

<b><big>Rooted Installe</big></b>r
Uses root access to install applications silently without requiring user confirmation. This method requires a rooted device, which may pose security risks and void warranties.

<b><big>Shizuku Installe</big></b>r
Utilizes the <a href="https://shizuku.rikka.app/">Shizuk</a>u service to grant system-level permissions without requiring full root access. It allows silent installations with user-granted privileges, offering a balance between automation and security. This method requires <a href="https://shizuku.rikka.app/download/">installin</a>g and <a href="https://shizuku.rikka.app/guide/setup/">setting up Shizuk</a>u beforehand.</string>
